<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aden Protectorate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1872">1872</a>–<a href="/years/1967">1967</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as British Aden Protectorate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> was the group of sultanates, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a> and sheikhdoms in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> bound to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> by treaties of protection around the port of Aden. Its border with Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> was fixed between 1904 and 1914, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imams</a> of Yemen later claimed it. Most of its states joined the Federation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabia</a> before independence as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a> in 1967.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aden-protectorate.jpg" alt="Aden Protectorate" width="320" height="315" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lubiesque · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aden_Colony_dependencies.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
